@startuml
title One folding step: from u on L to u_fold on L squared
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  DiamondBorderColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam ArrowColor #7A5BB5
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}

start
:Input: u from L to F, with L the n-th roots of unity
(n a power of two, so x in L implies -x in L);
:Verifier samples a random r in F;
:For each a in L, read the pair u(a), u(-a);
:Even part:  u_e(a^2) = (u(a) + u(-a)) / 2;
:Odd part:   u_o(a^2) = (u(a) - u(-a)) / (2a);
:u_fold(a^2) = u_e(a^2) + r * u_o(a^2);
:Output: u_fold from L^2 to F,  |L^2| = n / 2;
if (u was a codeword of degree < d ?) then (yes)
  :u_fold is a codeword of degree < d / 2 over L^2
  (same rate, for every r);<<#F3EEFB>>
else (no: u is delta-far, delta below the Johnson bound)
  :u_fold is delta-far from the compressed code
  with high probability over r;<<#FDEEEE>>
endif
stop
@enduml
